 "post": {
  "title": "3 settings that stop apps tracking you",
  "caption": "3 settings that stop apps tracking you 📍\n\n1. Location: While Using. Apps that say Always can read your location even when they are closed.\n2. Precise Location: off. Weather and shopping apps only need your area, not your front door.\n3. Ad tracking: off. On iPhone, apps then can't read the advertising ID that links you across apps; on Android, deleting the ID gives apps only zeros.\n\nTwo minutes, three switches. Save this for tonight, and send it to the friend who taps Allow on everything.",
  "keywords": [
   "stop apps tracking you",
   "phone privacy settings",
   "turn off precise location",
   "delete advertising ID android",
   "iPhone privacy settings",
   "phone settings to change"
  ],
  "hashtags": [
   "#privacytips",
   "#phonesettings",
   "#phonetips",
   "#iphonetips",
   "#androidtips"
  ],
  "sources": [
   {
    "url": "https://support.apple.com/en-us/102647",
    "note": "Apple Support, Location Services: While Using the App allows access only when the app or its features are visible on screen; turn Precise Location off to share only your approximate location"
   },
   {
    "url": "https://support.apple.com/en-us/102420",
    "note": "Apple Support, If an app asks to track your activity: with Allow Apps to Request to Track off, apps can't access the advertising identifier (IDFA); Settings > Privacy & Security > Tracking"
   },
   {
    "url": "https://developer.android.com/develop/sensors-and-location/location/permissions/runtime",
    "note": "Android Developers: users choose Precise or Approximate, and While using the app / Only this time / Deny"
   },
   {
    "url": "https://developer.android.com/develop/sensors-and-location/location/permissions",
    "note": "Android Developers: approximate location is accurate to within about 3 square kilometers; precise usually within about 50 meters"
   },
   {
    "url": "https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/6048248",
    "note": "Google Play Console Help, Advertising ID: when a user deletes the advertising ID (Settings > Privacy > Ads, Android 12+), apps reading it get a string of zeros"
   }
  ]
 },
